ent the weekly scan files carries `evidence/scan-finding.json`, not `detection.json`; `finding.read_any` maps it to metric `security: <class>`, rule `scan`, tier 3, and there are no failed-run URLs. Add one requirement: `detected` is read through `finding.read_any`, the `detection` source points at whichever file exists, `run-<n>` sources are absent for a scan incident, and the class tag is the scan's `class` field (item 1).\n10. Determinism the build would otherwise guess, write each down: the index line is `* [title](file) - description. Tier n, Mon yyyy.` (the proposal's); \"newest first\" sorts by `detected.at` descending, then file name; `## Unsorted` comes after `## Retired`; `build` with zero lessons writes the heading and one line \"No lessons yet.\"; the gate finds the lesson by `lessons/*-<slug>.md` (the month varies); the required fields are every field of the table except `runbook` and `supersedes`, which are optional; \"the eval case exists\" means `evals/cases/<id>-<slug>/prompt.md` and `checks.yaml` both exist. Acceptance says \"three sub-checks\" and lists five: make the count match.\n11. Restore these intent sentences the spec dropped, one Requirements bullet each: a stale lesson is still read and the maintain run says when it relied on one; `description` is one sentence in the metric's terms; a hand edit of the index is undone by the next `build`; `/sdlc-init` copies the README as today; no workflow template changes; the sample stays frozen; decision 17 unchanged.\n12. Add the `supersedes` rule to the deploy requirement: when the new lesson carries `supersedes: <file>`, step 0b sets the earlier lesson's `status: retired` and adds `retired_by: <the new file>` in the same commit; the gate (e) sub-check verifies the superseded file exists and reads `retired`.\n13. Both command files' `allowed-tools` frontmatter gains `Bash(python \"${CLAUDE_PLUGIN_ROOT}/plugin/lessons/index.py\" *)`, and the body quotes the call the same way (the instruction test requires it). CI is unaffected; a by-hand run would otherwise prompt.\n14. Citations to correct: `HANDOFF.md:60-61` is item 11 (item 4 is the row at line 42); `tests/test_evals.py:701-767` are the `case.py new` CLI tests, not instruction tests; `tests/test_gate.py:2346-2364` is gate (f) coverage, not (e), and no (e) incident fixture exists yet (say to build one with `_ctx(tmp_path, phase=\"e\")` and `entry_route=\"incident\"`); `docs/notes/1.md`'s frontmatter is flat (`generated.at` is one key).\n\n**plan.md**\n15. Add `plugin/lessons/__init__.py` to \"## Files that change\" (every plugin subpackage has one; the plan-sync exemption covers `*.md` only, so step 1's commit is denied without it).\n16. The \"No change to \u2026\" paragraph wraps so that one line starts with `17), to \\`plugin/detect/**\\``, and the gate's file-list parser reads it as a numbered item: `plugin/detect/**` is currently counted as a planned file (the opposite of the sentence, and the port-list path HANDOFF tracks). Move that paragraph to Risks and make sure no continuation line in \"## Files that change\" starts with a digit, `-` or `*`.\n17. Reflect items 2 to 13 in the file items: the phase guard and the separate check in the `checks.py` item and Risk 2; `build` excluding README and index, `--today`, the Unsorted rule, newline and `as_posix()` in the `index.py` item; the `supersedes` rule, the scan shape, block style and the `allowed-tools` line in the `sdlc-deploy.md` item; the `allowed-tools` line in the `sdlc-maintain.md` item.\n18. Tests: `tests/test_lessons.py` adds README.md present and ignored, index.md ignored, malformed frontmatter to Unsorted without a crash, a CRLF index on disk passing `check`, zero lessons, the stale marker with `--today`, class normalisation; `tests/test_gate.py` adds the (e) incident fixture, the pass case, one test per failure, the rendered what-I-need text, and the (f) regression; if `artifacts.py` needs the eval case names, import them from `plugin/evals/case.