roblem on its own indented line.\n4. The eval case's file names (plan.md's `artifacts.py` item): `plugin/evals/case.py` names `prompt.md` and `checks.yaml` as locals (`case.py:178`), not as constants, so \"import them if that module already names them as constants\" falls back to duplicating them, and adding constants to `case.py` would be a commit the plan-sync hook denies (it is not under \"## Files that change\", and Risk 1 says it does not change). Decided: the two names are constants in `plugin/gate/artifacts.py` beside the lesson's required fields, with a one-line comment naming `case.py:178` as the writer that must agree; `case.py` stays untouched. Drop the conditional.\n5. The eval case in every section (spec.md Design, Acceptance; plan.md's `checks.py` and `test_gate.py` items, Order of work step 2, Risk 2, Proof): Requirements say \"both `prompt.md` and `checks.yaml` exist\", the other sections say \"the eval case folder exists\" and the fail case is \"missing eval case folder\". Use the Requirements meaning everywhere; the fail case is \"`prompt.md` or `checks.yaml` missing\".\n\n**spec.md: the sentences the first review asked for**\n6. Item 7 asked for a requirement: add one Requirements bullet stating that the index is written with `write_text(..., newline=\"\\n\")`, that `check` compares text read in universal-newline mode, and that every link is rendered with the native path's `.as_posix()` (`Path(...).as_posix()`, as `case.py:181` does; `PurePosixPath(str(p)).as_posix()` keeps a backslash from a Windows path).\n7. Item 5 asked that an `## Unsorted` entry does not fail `check`: add the sentence \u2014 `check` exits 0 with `## Unsorted` entries present and prints one note line per Unsorted file; only a drift of the generated text is exit 1. Reword the README bullet's \"reported by `check`\" to say the same.\n8. Item 4 asked for `--today` under Acceptance: add it there, with the class-normalisation test.\n9. Item 9 asked that the `detection` source points at whichever file exists: in the `sources` sentence of Requirements bullet 1, say the `detection` resource is `evidence/detection.json`, or `evidence/scan-finding.json` for an incident the weekly scan filed. Replace \"read through `plugin/detect/finding.read_any`\" with \"with the mapping `finding.read_any` implements (`finding.py:150-160`)\": step 0b is instruction text for the model, nothing in the plan calls that function.\n10. Item 13 asked for the `allowed-tools` lines in spec.md too: one Requirements bullet naming `Bash(python \"${CLAUDE_PLUGIN_ROOT}/plugin/lessons/index.py\" *)` for both command files and the body's call quoted the same way.\n11. Item 11 asked for one Requirements bullet per restored sentence; they are present but folded into other bullets. Give each its own bullet.\n\n**spec.md: determinism the build would otherwise guess**\n12. Write down: the index opens with `# Lessons` and no frontmatter (nothing reads one); tag headings are ordered alphabetically by the normalised class; the link is the file name relative to `lessons/` (`(2026-10-<slug>.md)`); \"Mon yyyy\" is `detected.at`'s month; `description` carries no trailing period (the line adds it); an `## Unsorted` line is `* [first heading](file)` and a `## Retired` line has the tag line's shape; `(stale)` is appended at the end of the line, on `## Retired` lines too.\n13. The required frontmatter fields, by name: `type`, `title`, `description`, `tags`, `change`, `detected`, `fixed`, `generated`, `status`, `stale_after`, `sources`; `runbook`, `supersedes` and `retired_by` are optional (the current sentence \"every field named in the first Requirements bullet except `runbook` and `supersedes`\" would make `retired_by` required on every new lesson).\n14. The gate's glob: `lessons/[0-9][0-9][0-9][0-9]-[0-9][0-9]-<slug>.md`, so a slug that ends in another change's slug does not match; more than one match fails the check.\n\n**plan.md**\n15. Order of work step 1 names `plugin/lessons/__init__.py` (it is why the file was added).\n16. `tests/test_gate.py`: one unit test calls `lesson_and_eval` with a phase (f) incident context and asserts it passes, so the guard itself is proven, not only the registration.\n17. Citations: `HANDOFF.md:42` is item 2b on `main` since PR #126 (item 4 is line 39) \u2014 cite it as \"HANDOFF.md, item 4\" with no line; `CHECKS_BY_PHASE[\"e\"]` is `checks.py:1646-1660`; Risk 5's \"skips exactly one\" is wrong (`yamlish.loads` skips every `---` before the first content line, and a `---` after content raises `expected 'key: value'`), the conclusion stands.\n\n---\n_Generated by [Claude Code](https://claude.ai/code)_",
