+      "signature": "68c603a585c7aa94",
+      "summary": "`_supersedes_problem` only validates `supersedes` when its value is already a string (`isinstance(supersedes, str)`); a present-but-non-string value (a list or a number) returns `None` and is silently treated as \"no supersedes\" instead of being reported as malformed."
+    },
+    {
+      "file": "plugin/lessons/index.py",
+      "line": 231,
+      "pass": "bugs",
+      "rule": "doubt stated: cosmetic breakage of a generated markdown file, not a functional break \u2014 `/sdlc-maintain` matches lessons by heading/tags, not by parsing the link text.",
+      "severity": "nit",
+      "signature": "fae254b0a97e5724",
+      "summary": "`_render_line`/`_render_unsorted_line` interpolate `title`, `description` and the first heading into a markdown link (`[text](file)`) with no escaping of `]`/`(`/`)`, so a value containing one of those characters breaks the generated link in `lessons/index.md`."
+    },
